    {
      "id": "navigation",
      "name": "Navigation",
      "version": "2.9.6",
      "url": "https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/navigation#2.9.6",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>Bug Fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li>The Navigation <code>SafeArgs</code> plugin has been migrated to the modern Android Gradle Plugin APIs which should ensure it is compatible with all AGP 8.4.2+ releases. As a result of these changes, the output directory for files generated by the plugin has been changed to the default location provided by AGP. (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/Ie09d6947cd45dba0c9300d1c5d6f5c100bb0f736\">Ie09d6</a>, <a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I7c431915405539e350c26c49ce7b62782ba9fa6d\">I7c431</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/203559535\">b/203559535</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/293920476\">b/293920476</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/269532448\">b/269532448</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/443261197\">b/443261197</a>)</li>\n <li>Navigation <code>SafeArgs</code> plugin will no longer require setting the <code>useAndroidX</code> property when being used with AGP 9.0.0-alpha04+. (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I6c3a4eecab1c0927d72742952acdf4aa135b7c7e\">I6c3a4</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/444746731\">b/444746731</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/443106400\">b/443106400</a>)</li>\n</ul>",
      "commitsUrl": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+log/312fd656536cad70baa4b54621f396d2bd72543f..35a9607626f7b80b5418beb35a698f22307e6be3/navigation"
    },
    {
      "id": "navigation3",
      "name": "Navigation3",
      "version": "1.0.0-rc01",
      "url": "https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/navigation3#1.0.0-rc01",
      "detailsHtml": "<p><strong>Bug Fixes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n <li><code>NavDisplay</code> now sets a <code>LocalLifecycleOwner</code> at the <code>Scene</code> level that allows scene authors to determine whether all transitions have finished by checking that the <code>Lifecycle.State</code> is <code>RESUMED</code>. The behavior of the <code>LocalLifecycleOwner</code> at the <code>NavEntry</code> level is unchanged: it also remains capped at <code>STARTED</code> if a transition is in progress and is additionally capped at <code>CREATED</code> if that <code>NavEntry</code> has been popped from the back stack and is in the process of animating out. (<a href=\"https://android-review.googlesource.com/#/q/I03113a4729d59a9d2bc09d4422d41615f60ab935\">I03113</a>, <a href=\"https://issuetracker.google.com/issues/454045829\">b/454045829</a>)</li>\n</ul>",
      "commitsUrl": "https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/+log/46bcdef6281ae0f03c3a2bb2812edfc2c0e66d05..ebd829d61998c48ea35b0e2adbc801d9c5ae36cc/navigation3"
    },
